<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<scheme version="2.0" title="Ch.5 predicting an unknown (acetic acid NIR)" description="A: 1 mm -&gt; SG 9/2/d2 -&gt; 2258.067 nm only; hide the 4.87 % bottle, Linear Regression on the other 3, Predictions for the hidden bottle. B: 4 calibration signals (x1e3) + one unknown y0 = 4.20 from unknown_2258_orange.csv, Linear Regression on 4, Predictions for the unknown. Orange's regression is direct (conc = a + b*signal) and gives a point prediction only; the lesson's inverse calibration and Fieller interval are in R / Python. Data: ../../data/spectra_wide_orange.csv, ../../data/unknown_2258_orange.csv">
